    "result_text": "All 17 tests pass, including the new `Cp09Tests`. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented server-assigned `customerCode` on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 a pipeline step that mutates the built owner in place, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (safe for names shorter than 3).\n   - `NNNN` = `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`SMI-0007`).\n\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `customerCode` step into the create pipeline between `registrationDate` and `save`, under the existing `transaction` governance.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in `GET /api/owners/{id}` (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n\n5. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 ignored `customerCode` in `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` so the request body can't set it (it's server-assigned).\n\n6. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column so the entity persists cleanly across all supported databases.\n\nBecause the code is computed before save from the live owner count, each subsequent create sees the prior one committed, so the global sequence increments by one (verified by the test: `SMI-000N` then `JON-000(N+1)`).",
